# 9. WEEKLY ATTENDANCE SYSTEM

Build a real QR-based attendance system.

This is a core feature, not a visual simulation.

## Admin creates a session

Fields:

- Session title.
- Description.
- Session date.
- Starting time.
- Ending time.
- Location.
- Organizer.
- Target participants.
- Attendance opening time.
- Late threshold.
- Attendance closing time.
- QR rotation interval.
- Session status.

Statuses:

Draft / Scheduled / Open / Closed / Cancelled.

## Dynamic QR attendance

The administrator opens a session and projects a QR code.

The QR code should rotate approximately every 20–30 seconds, configurable by the administrator.

Each token should include or reference:

- Session identifier.
- Issued time.
- Expiration time.
- Cryptographically secure signature or opaque server-generated token.

Validate the token server-side.

Never trust client-supplied timestamps.

Do not expose secret signing keys in frontend code.

## Member check-in workflow

1. Member signs in.
2. Member scans the QR code using the phone camera or follows its check-in link.
3. App checks authentication.
4. Server validates the token.
5. Server verifies the member is eligible.
6. Server checks the attendance window.
7. Server checks for duplicate attendance.
8. Attendance is stored atomically.
9. Member receives a success or informative error message.

Use consistent server timestamps.

One member can have at most one active attendance record per session.

## Attendance statuses

- Present.
- Late.
- Excused absence.
- Unexcused absence.
- Pending review.

Allow administrators to approve excused absences and manually correct records.

Every manual correction must capture:

- Previous status.
- New status.
- Administrator identity.
- Timestamp.
- Reason.

Important: rotating QR codes reduce casual misuse but cannot eliminate all forms of remote sharing.

Do not falsely describe the system as completely preventing proxy attendance.

Provide optional in-person verification by a session organizer.

## Attendance dashboard

Show:

- Eligible members.
- Checked-in members.
- Attendance rate.
- Late arrivals.
- Approved absences.
- Missing attendance records.

Allow filtering by sessions, committees and time periods.

Export CSV data compatible with Excel.

Support UTF-8 encoding and proper Vietnamese characters.

